---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "@/components/Icon.astro";
import { site } from "@/data/site";
import { withBase } from "@/lib/url";
---

<Base
  title="Portable Neural Recording"
  description="A wearable device for continuous neural recording from implanted DBS electrodes during the two-week gap between surgeries."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 pt-36 pb-24 sm:px-12 md:px-24">
    <a
      href={withBase("/#projects")}
      class="font-mono text-muted hover:text-accent inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs transition-colors"
    >
      <Icon name="arrow" size={14} class="rotate-180" /> back to portfolio
    </a>

    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mt-8 mb-12" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">STRIVE Medical · UMN Neurology · In Progress</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">Portable Neural Recording</h1>
      <p class="text-muted mt-2 text-lg">Closing the Two-Week Gap in Brain Stimulation</p>
      <p class="text-accent mt-3 text-sm font-medium">
        Team of 7 · Clinical Collaboration · Hardware Design
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-[var(--color-accent)] bg-[var(--color-accent)]/10 px-3 py-1">
        <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] animate-pulse"></span>
        <span class="text-accent text-xs font-medium">Active Development</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Hero Image -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-lg overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)]">
        <img
          src={withBase("/media/portable-eeg-cover.jpg")}
          alt="Deep brain stimulation electrode placement"
          class="w-full"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Problem -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">The Problem</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        Deep brain stimulation (DBS) can treat epilepsy, depression, OCD, and other neurological
        conditions, but the way it's implanted in the US leaves a critical gap. The procedure
        happens in two separate surgeries: first the electrodes are placed in the brain, then
        about two weeks later a second surgery connects them to a pulse generator in the chest.
        For those two weeks, the implanted electrodes sit idle and record nothing, while patients
        stay tethered to bulky hospital equipment.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body mb-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        That window is a missed opportunity. It's exactly when doctors could be learning how a
        patient's brain behaves in real life, rather than in a hospital bed. And there's a deeper
        limitation: today a surgeon commits to a single stimulation target with no way to test it
        first, and roughly half of DBS cases don't deliver the results patients hope for.
        Conditions like depression and OCD make this even harder, because their symptoms rarely
        appear in a clinical setting.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        For patients who can't be treated with medication alone, current reimbursement programs
        don't allow stereo EEG, the gold standard for understanding where neural issues
        originate. This device closes that gap.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- What We're Building -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">What We're Building</h2>
      <p class="text-body mb-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        We're developing a portable, wearable recording device that captures continuous neural
        data from implanted electrodes during that two-week window, at home, in the patient's
        normal environment. Instead of staying wired to a hospital machine, patients go home with
        a compact box that records around the clock.
      </p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-6">
          <h3 class="text-heading mb-2 text-base font-semibold">The Anchor</h3>
          <p class="text-body text-[0.85rem]">
            A secure interface that stabilizes the electrodes where they exit the skull, so
            signals stay clean during everyday movement.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-6">
          <h3 class="text-heading mb-2 text-base font-semibold">The Recorder</h3>
          <p class="text-body text-[0.85rem]">
            A miniaturized, low-power device that reliably captures 24-hour neural data while
            managing battery life, onboard storage, and signal noise.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Where It Leads -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Where It Leads</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        Longer term, this becomes a platform. If electrodes can be placed at several candidate
        targets and trialed at home, clinicians could find the target that actually works best
        for each patient before committing to a permanent implant, then remove the rest. That
        has the potential to meaningfully raise DBS success rates and extend the approach well
        beyond epilepsy to depression, OCD, and any condition that depends on capturing
        real-world neural signals.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Clinical Partners -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Clinical Partners</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-6">
          <h3 class="text-heading mb-2 text-base font-semibold">UMN Visible Heart Lab</h3>
          <p class="text-body text-[0.85rem]">
            A world-recognized research lab providing expertise in medical device development,
            testing infrastructure, and translational research methodology.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-line)] bg-[var(--color-bg-raised)] p-6">
          <h3 class="text-heading mb-2 text-base font-semibold">UMN Neurology Department</h3>
          <p class="text-body text-[0.85rem]">
            Clinical neurology faculty defining the recording requirements, access to DBS
            patients and workflows, and validation of captured neural data quality.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Current Status -->
    <section class="mb-14" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-heading mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Current Status</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
        A team of seven is actively developing the device. The anchor interface and recorder
        architecture are in early design, with clinical requirements defined alongside the UMN
        Neurology department. More details will be published as the project progresses.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Tech chips -->
    <div class="border-line flex flex-wrap gap-3 border-t pt-8" data-reveal>
      {["Neural Recording", "DBS", "Analog Front End", "PCB Design", "Signal Processing", "Altium", "Low Power", "Biomedical"].map(t => (
        <span class="chip">{t}</span>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
